            <ArticleTitle>Coronary vein angioplasty with noncompliant balloon for resistant coronary vein stenosis during left ventricular lead implantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>251-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8159.2007.00978.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a patient who underwent cardiac resynchronization therapy (CRT) in the setting of a severe stenosis in the lateral coronary vein that prevented passage of a left ventricular lead. The stenosis was unresponsive to standard compliant balloon dilatation but was successfully treated with a noncompliant balloon. Venoplasty with noncompliant balloon should be considered for resistant coronary vein stenosis encountered during CRT device implantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
